From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump klauspost/compress to v1.20.2 for CVE-2026-116591

Upstream: https://github.com/klauspost/compress/releases/tag/v1.20.2

readNCount accepted a normalized FSE count of 32768, stored as int16
-32768, so huff0.ReadTable built a Huffman-weights decode table that
kept the previous blocks stale fse.Scratch state. zstd DecodeAll and
the streaming decoder reused that stale state across a crafted
two-block frame and indexed past the table, panicking on untrusted
input. Fixed by rejecting counts that cannot fit the table before
they are truncated, and by capping the FSE tableLog of Huffman
weights at 6 per RFC 8878.

Match go-vendor-tools.toml pre_command that runs
  go get github.com/klauspost/compress@v1.20.2
Keep go.mod/go.sum in the source tree in sync with the regenerated
vendor.
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -528,7 +528,7 @@
 	github.com/jpillora/backoff v1.0.0 // indirect
 	github.com/jszwedko/go-datemath v0.1.1-0.20230526204004-640a500621d6 // indirect
 	github.com/jtolds/gls v4.20.0+incompatible // indirect
-	github.com/klauspost/compress v1.19.1 // indirect
+	github.com/klauspost/compress v1.20.2 // indirect
 	github.com/klauspost/cpuid/v2 v2.3.0 // indirect
 	github.com/kylelemons/godebug v1.1.0 // indirect
 	github.com/lann/builder v0.0.0-20180802200727-47ae307949d0 // indirect
